            <ArticleTitle>Synthesis of 3-(2-Olefinbenzyl)-4H-chromen-4-one through Cyclobenzylation and Catalytic C-H Bond Functionalization Using Palladium(II).</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>10855-10865</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1021/acs.joc.7b01626</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>An efficient strategy for synthesizing 3-(2-olefinbenzyl)-4H-chromen-4-one in two steps was developed. The first step is a cyclobenzylation reaction between (E)-3-(dimethylamino)-1-(2-hydroxyphenyl)prop-2-en-1-one and benzyl bromide to produce homoisoflavonoid. The second step involves intermolecular Pd-catalyzed π-chelating-assisted C-H bond olefination. Using the C-2/C-3 double bond of chromone, palladium-catalyzed aryl C-H bond activation can be functionalized to generate ortho-olefination derivatives in moderate to high yields.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
